Z||000002||artherd||11-14-2001||02:42 AM||||Because we needed something that's not a Northstar with same engine's proven reliability record and huge untaped power potential?<P>That looks like an EPA wet-dream motor.  (only reason for a 3-valve motor is for fast converter lightoff. Blah.)<P>"Displacement on Demand" sounds like another disaster in the making.   Even if it does work, suddenly running on 4 cylinders is just going to be less than smooth.<P>My verdict? why the &*#$ bother.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by avengador1:<BR><B>It's supposed to be as wide as a V6 and as long as a I4.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GM-V-8.jpg">  sorry it's so big, I have to figure out how to shrink it.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||Raydar||11-14-2001||10:48 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>...only reason for a 3-valve motor is for fast converter lightoff. Blah.<P>"Displacement on Demand" sounds like another disaster in the making.   Even if it does work, suddenly running on 4 cylinders is just going to be less than smooth.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>What about a "staged" intake, like the LT-5?<BR>The primary intake system feeds one valve. When the secondary system opens, it feeds both. It's a way to keep the velocity up without limiting the volume.<P>Also, it seems to me that the "Northstar System" already uses a version of displacement on demand. If the coolant is drained, the engine will run on four cylinders, then the other four cylinders, allowing cooling air to be pulled through on every other series of revs. Should be really easy to do with electronics. I'll bet they can tweak it to make it run smoothly.<BR>I agree that the 8-6-4 system with it's solenoids and stuff was a mechanical abortion of the highest order.<P>Am I wrong?<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
